.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt PRIME_IMPORT_PROBE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm prime_import_probe
.Nd test cross-GPU buffer import between two DRM devices
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -json | Fl -jsonl
.Op Fl s Ar WxH
.Ar src
.Ar dst
.Nm
.Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility creates a dumb buffer on the DRM device
.Ar src ,
fills it with a pattern, exports it as a dma-buf, imports it on the DRM
device
.Ar dst
and adds a framebuffer for the imported handle.
It reports the result of every step.
It never sets a mode and never changes a CRTC, so it does not disturb a
running display.
.Pp
It is the probe behind section 5.2 of the cross-GPU import design
.Pq Pa docs/PRIME-IMPORT.md
in the nvidia-gb10-freebsd tree: with
.Ar src
an amdgpu device and
.Ar dst
an nvidia-drm device, a system-memory buffer must import and
.Dq Fn drmModeAddFB2
must return, either with success or with a clean errno.
A kernel panic, a hang or a signal is the failure.
Run it a second time with the two arguments swapped to see the other
direction.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -json
Write one JSON document, an object with a
.Li rows
array, to standard output.
.It Fl -jsonl
Write one JSON object per buffer size, one per line, each flushed as it is
produced.
This is also the default.
.It Fl s Ar WxH
Test a dumb buffer of
.Ar W
by
.Ar H
pixels, 32 bits per pixel, each from 1 to 16384.
The option may be repeated, up to 16 times.
The default is 64x64 and 1920x1080.
.It Fl -help
Print a usage message and exit.
.El
.Pp
Every object names its schema,
.Li prime-import-probe/1 ,
which is
.Pa tests/prime-import-testboot/prime-import-probe.schema.json
in the source tree.
The fields
.Li create ,
.Li map ,
.Li fill ,
.Li export ,
.Li import
and
.Li addfb
are 0 when the step succeeded and \-1 when it failed or was not tried.
.Li stage
is the step the probe stopped in,
.Li done
when every step ran, and
.Li errno
and
.Li error
describe the first failure.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
In detail: 0 when every step returned, whether with success or an errno;
2 on a usage error;
3 when a device cannot be opened.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
After a run, two read-only variables of
.Xr nvidia 4
describe the release path of imported buffers (see section 7.6 of
docs/PRIME-IMPORT.md):
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Va hw.nvidia_unlock_dirty_refused
Pages with a VM object that were not all valid when the RM unpinned them, and so were not marked dirty.
Must read 0; a nonzero value is a driver defect and the boot kit fails the run.
.It Va hw.nvidia_unlock_dirty_busy_fallback
Pages the RM unpinned while their busy lock stayed held through a short spin; they were marked dirty without it.
Reported by the boot kit as information.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Import a buffer from the first card on the second one, for two sizes:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
prime_import_probe --jsonl -s 256x256 -s 1920x1080 \e
    /dev/dri/card0 /dev/dri/card1
.Ed
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility was written for Track #2228 in 2026.
